      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "DIFFORUM - PARALLAX + FLUIDITY\n\nTwo fixes for \"static and choppy\", wired together.\n\n1. PARALLAX (fixes static)\n   Without a depth map the Feedback Sampler silently falls back to a 2D\n   affine warp - every pixel moves identically and the frame reads as a\n   photo being pushed around. Depth Anything V2 supplies the depth, so\n   warp_3d runs and near pixels travel faster than far ones.\n   - Camera Keys mode must stay 3d\n   - translation_scale 1.6 on the sampler exaggerates the parallax\n   - near 0.6 / far 40 tightens the depth range onto the actual scene\n   Write prompts with layers: something close, something far. Depth has\n   nothing to work with in a flat image.\n\n2. FLUIDITY (fixes choppy)\n   cadence 2 means content really changes at 12fps. RIFE interpolates\n   2x, so the MP4 runs at 48fps with motion-compensated in-betweens\n   rather than warp slides. Raise the multiplier to 3-4 for projection.\n\n3. ANTI-CONVERGENCE\n   The old settings settled into a fixed pattern. Changed:\n   - color_coherence 0.80 -> 0.60   (less pull back to the anchor)\n   - strength_bias +0.08            (the loop keeps evolving)\n   - camera_scale 1.6               (gives the sampler something to bite)\n   - noise 0.025 -> 0.035, sharpen 0.30\n   - flow_align strength 0.5 -> 0.35 (over-stabilising also freezes it)\n\nFIRST RUN downloads the depth model (~50MB vitb) and the RIFE weights\n(~50MB). Both are automatic.\n\nWORKFLOW\n   Run once and read the Storyboard + Depth check before anything else.\n   Storyboard info reports \"drift avg\" - below 0.004 means it will\n   stagnate, so raise camera_scale. The Depth check should show clear\n   near/far separation; a flat grey map means the prompt has no depth.\n\nAPPLE SILICON\n   RIFE runs on MPS. If it fails, set scale_factor 0.5.\n   No fp8 anywhere - MPS has no fp8 kernel."
      ],
      "title": "READ THIS",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
